fact WorkItem(id: "WI-735", description: some(value: "WI-714/WI-727 follow-up: fix -- accept NON-LITERAL constant arguments (a const-folded expression / a term-level const binding), beyond the literal Int/Float/Bool/String the first increment allows. CONTEXT: proposal 052 'fix is sugar' + proposal 056 (variadic capture), delivered as WI-727 (94dbe449). 'r.fix(x: 1, z: 2)' restricts columns to constants and DROPS them (= where(eq(x,1)) + project). fix is an ORDINARY operation -- 'operation fix[R](p: Relation, ...args: R) -> Relation[T = Without[T = p.T, Drop = R], E = p.E]' -- whose dynamic column arguments ride the ...args: R variadic capture into a named-tuple record; the host builtin (relation_fix) reads the args record VALUE and wraps guarded(query, eq(col, const)) per captured field, then drops the column (which stays SOLVED in the query = bag semantics, like project). SCOPE of the first increment: LITERAL constants only. GAP: a captured arg that is a const-folded expression or a term-level const (proposal 039 / WI-084, which already carries a LOAD-time purity gate) is rejected even though it is statically a constant. FIX DIRECTION: relax the constant check to accept any value the const/purity machinery already certifies as a compile-time constant -- REUSE WI-084's existing gate rather than adding a second notion of constant-ness; the eq is a GUARDED SEMANTIC eq (PartialEq.eq, WI-616), so any value with a lawful eq works at runtime; the constraint is about compile-time knowability, not the eq. Keep the Without[T, Drop] membership + constant-TYPE checks as the LOAD errors, and keep NOTHING keyed on fix's identity in the typer (the feedback-typer-no-nongeneric-code discipline -- the op_sym == Relation.fix recognizer was explicitly rejected by the user and removed). ACCEPTANCE: 'r.fix(age: someConstOp())' / a term-level const binding restricts + drops correctly end-to-end; a non-constant (a runtime value) stays a LOUD load error naming why; existing wi727_fix tests (11) green; cargo-test green via scripts/test.sh."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-714", "WI-727"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Open)
